G5405.b:
⟪Φοῖνιξ⟫, -ικος, ο, ἡ
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a Phœnician⟫ (also with fem., Φοίνισσα, Hom., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪Phœnix⟫, a city of Crete: ⟦Acts 27:12|Ac 27:12⟧.†

G5438.b:
⟪φυλακή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ
(< φυλάσσω) [in LXX chiefly for ⁨מִשְׁמֶרֶת⁩ and cogn. forms, also for ⁨כֶּלֶא⁩ etc. ;]
⟪(a)⟫ actively, ⟪a guarding, guard, watch⟫ (Hom., Plat., Xen., al.): cogn. acc., φυλάσσειν φυλακάς, ⟪to keep watch⟫, ⟦Luke 2:8|Lk 2:8⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of those who keep watch (as also Lat. custodia), ⟪a guard⟫; pl., ⟪sentinels, a guard⟫ (Hom., al.): ⟦Acts 12:10|Ac 12:10⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of the place where persons are kept under guard, ⟪a prison⟫ (Hdt., Thuc., al.): ⟦Matthew 14:10|Mt 14:10⟧, ⟦Mark 6:17|Mk 6:17⟧, ⟦Luke 3:20|Lk 3:20⟧, ⟦Acts 5:19|Ac 5:19⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:5|II Co 6:5⟧, ⟦1 Peter 3:19|I Pe 3:19⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:2|Re 18:2⟧, al.;
⟪(d)⟫ of the time during which guard was kept by night (Lat. vigilia; Anthol.), ⟪a watch⟫: ⟦Matthew 14:25|Mt 14:25⟧ ⟦Matthew 24:43|24:43⟧, ⟦Mark 6:48|Mk 6:48⟧, ⟦Luke 12:38|Lk 12:38⟧

G5442.b:
⟪φυλάσσω⟫
[in LXX chiefly and very freq. for ⁨שָׁמַר⁩, also for ⁨נָצַר⁩, etc. ;] ⟪to guard, watch⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to guard⟫ or ⟪watch⟫: c. cogn. acc., φυλακάς, ⟦Luke 2:8|Lk 2:8⟧; c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 12:4|Ac 12:4⟧ ⟦Acts 28:16|28:16⟧; pass., ⟦Luke 8:29|Lk 8:29⟧, ⟦Acts 23:35|Ac 23:35⟧; c. acc. rei, ⟦Acts 22:20|Ac 22:20⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to guard⟫or ⟪protect⟫: c. acc., ⟦Luke 11:21|Lk 11:21⟧, ⟦John 12:25|Jo 12:25⟧ ⟦John 17:12|17:12⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:3|II Th 3:3⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 6:20|I Ti 6:20⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:12|II Ti 1:12⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:14|14⟧, ⟦2 Peter 2:5|II Pe 2:5⟧; ἑαυτὸν ἀπό, ⟦1 John 5:21|I Jo 5:21⟧ (Westc., in l.); metaph. of law, precept, etc., ⟪to keep, preserve, observe⟫: ⟦Matthew 19:20|Mt 19:20⟧, ⟦Luke 11:28|Lk 11:28⟧ ⟦Luke 18:21|18:21⟧, ⟦John 12:47|Jo 12:47⟧, ⟦Acts 7:53|Ac 7:53⟧ ⟦Acts 16:4|16:4⟧ ⟦Acts 21:24|21:24⟧, ⟦Romans 2:26|Ro 2:26⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:13|Ga 6:13⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:21|I Ti 5:21⟧. Mid., ⟪to be on one's guard⟫ (against), ⟪keep oneself from, beware of⟫: c. acc., ⟦Acts 21:25|Ac 21:25⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 4:15|II Ti 4:15⟧; seq. ἀπό., ⟦Luke 12:15|Lk 12:15⟧; ἵνα μή, ⟦2 Peter 3:17|II Pe 3:17⟧; as in LXX (⟦Exodus 12:17|Ex 12:17⟧, ⟦Leviticus 18:4|Le 18:4⟧, al.), of laws, etc., ⟪to keep, observe⟫: ταῦτα πάντα, ⟦Mark 10:20|Mk 10:20⟧ (cf. δια-φυάσσω).†
SYN.: τηρέω, q.v

G5446.b:
* ⟪φυσικός⟫, -ή, -όν
(< φύσις), ⟪natural⟫
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪produced by nature, innate⟫ (Xen., Arist., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪according to nature⟫ (Arist., Diod., al.): opp. to παρὰ φύσιν, ⟦Romans 1:26|Ro 1:26⟧, ⟦Romans 1:27|27⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪governed by mere natural instinct⟫ (cf. Plut., Mor., 706A): ζῷα γεγεννημένα φ. (RV,⟪born mere animals⟫; Mayor,⟪born creatures of instinct⟫; ICC, ⟪animals born of mere nature⟫), ⟦2 Peter 2:12|II Pe 2:12⟧,†

G5449.b:
** ⟪φύσις⟫, -εως, ἡ
(< φύω) [in LXX: Wi 7:20 13:1 19:20 אΑ, III Mac 3:29, IV Mac 1:20 5:7, 8, 25 13:27 15:13, 25 16:3 * ;] ⟪nature⟫, i.e.,
⟪(a)⟫ the ⟪nature⟫ (natural powers or constitution) of a person or thing: ⟦James 3:7|Ja 3:7⟧, ⟦2 Peter 1:4|II Pe 1:4⟧; τέκνα φυσει ὀργῆς, ⟦Ephesians 2:3|Eph 2:3⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪origin, birth⟫ (Soph., Xen., al.): ⟦Romans 2:27|Ro 2:27⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:15|Ga 2:15⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪nature⟫, i.e. the regular order or law of nature: ⟦1 Corinthians 11:14|I Co 11:14⟧; dat., φύσει adverbially, ⟪by nature⟫, ⟦Romans 2:14|Ro 2:14⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:8|Ga 4:8⟧; παρὰ φύσιν, ⟪against nature⟫, ⟦Romans 1:26|Ro 1:26⟧ ⟦Romans 11:24|11:24⟧; καρὰ φ., ⟪according to nature, naturally⟫, ⟦Romans 11:21|Ro 11:21⟧, ⟦Romans 11:24|24⟧.†

G5456.b:
⟪φωνή⟫, -ῆς, ἡ,
[in LXX chiefly and very freq. for ⁨קוֺל⁩ ;] ⟪a voice⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ prop., of persons, ⟦Matthew 2:18|Mt 2:18⟧ (LXX), al.; φ. αἴρειν (ἐπαίρειν), ⟦Luke 17:13|Lk 17:13⟧, ⟦Acts 2:14|Ac 2:14⟧, al.; φ. μεγάλῃ εἰπεῖν (λέγειν, φωνεῖν, etc.), ⟦Luke 8:28|Lk 8:28⟧, ⟦Acts 7:57|Ac 7:57⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:12|Re 5:12⟧, al.; γίνεται (ἔρχεται) φ. ἐκ τ. οὐρανῶν (ἐξ οὐρανοῦ), ⟦Mark 1:11|Mk 1:11⟧, ⟦Luke 3:22|Lk 3:22⟧, ⟦John 12:28|Jo 12:28⟧, al. (cf. DCG, ii, 810a; Dalman, Words, 204 f.); ἀκούειν φωνήν (-ῆς; v.s. ἀκούω), ⟦Acts 9:4|Ac 9:4⟧, ⟦Acts 9:7|7⟧ al.; φ. βοῶντος, ⟦Matthew 3:3|Mt 3:3⟧, ⟦Mark 1:3|Mk 1:3⟧, ⟦Luke 3:4|Lk 3:4⟧, ⟦John 1:23|Jo 1:23⟧ (LXX); τ. θεοῦ, ⟦John 5:37|Jo 5:37⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:7|He 3:7⟧, al. By meton.,
	⟪(α)⟫ of the speaker, βλέπειν τὴν φ., ⟦Revelation 1:12|Re 1:12⟧;
	⟪(β)⟫ ⟪speech, language⟫ ( ⟦Genesis 11:1|Ge 11:1⟧, IV Mac 12:7, al.): ⟦1 Corinthians 14:10|I Co 14:10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of inanimate things: ⟦Matthew 24:31|Mt 24:31⟧, ⟦John 3:8|Jo 3:8⟧, ⟦Acts 2:6|Ac 2:6⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:15|Re 1:15b⟧ ⟦Revelation 9:9|9:9⟧ ⟦Revelation 14:2|14:2⟧, al. (cf. Tr., Syn., § lxxxix).

G5457.b:
⟪φῶς⟫ (Att.. contr. from φάος; < φάω), gen., φωτός, τό,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨אוֹר⁩ ;] ⟪light⟫ (opp. to τὸ σκότος, ἡ σκοτία): ⟦Matthew 17:2|Mt 17:2⟧, ⟦Matthew 17:5|5⟧, ⟦John 11:9|Jo 11:9⟧, ⟦John 11:10|10⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:6|II Co 4:6⟧; ἡλίου, ⟦Revelation 22:5|Re 22:5⟧; of a lamp, ⟦Luke 8:16|Lk 8:16⟧ ⟦Luke 11:33|11:33⟧, ⟦John 5:35|Jo 5:35⟧, ⟦Revelation 18:23|Re 18:23⟧; of a supernatural heavenly light, ⟦Acts 9:3|Ac 9:3⟧ ⟦Acts 12:7|12:7⟧ ⟦Acts 22:6|22:6⟧, ⟦Acts 22:9|9⟧, ⟦Acts 22:11|11⟧ ⟦Acts 26:13|26:13⟧; hence, ἄγγελος φωτός, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:14|II Co 11:14⟧; ὁ κλήρος τ. ἁγίων ἐν τ. φ., ⟦Colossians 1:12|Col 1:12⟧; of the divine glory, ⟦Revelation 21:24|Re 21:24⟧; by meton., of that which gives light: of fire, ⟦Mark 14:54|Mk 14:54⟧, ⟦Luke 22:56|Lk 22:56⟧ (cl.; I Mac 12:29; cf. DCG, i, 595); pl., of a lamp or torch, ⟦Acts 16:29|Ac 16:29⟧; of heavenly bodies, ⟦James 1:17|Ja 1:17⟧. Metaph.,
⟪(a)⟫ of God: ⟦1 John 1:5|I Jo 1:5⟧, ⟦1 John 1:7|7⟧; φῶς οἰκῶν ἀπρόσιτον, ⟦1 Timothy 6:16|I Ti 6:16⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of spiritual truth and its effects on the lives of men: ⟦Matthew 4:16|Mt 4:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 5:16|5:16⟧, ⟦John 1:4|Jo 1:4⟧, ⟦John 1:5|5⟧ ⟦John 3:19|3:19-21⟧, ⟦Acts 26:18|Ac 26:18⟧, ⟦Acts 26:23|23⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:14|II Co 6:14⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:13|Eph 5:13⟧, ⟦1 Peter 2:9|I Pe 2:9⟧, ⟦1 John 2:8|I Jo 2:8⟧; τ. φ. τ. ζωῆς, ⟦John 8:12|Jo 8:12⟧; τ. ὅπλα τοῦ φ., ⟦Romans 13:12|Ro 13:12⟧; καρπὸς τοῦ φ., ⟦Ephesians 5:9|Eph 5:9⟧; έν τ. φ. περιπατεῖν (εἶναι, μένειν), ⟦1 John 1:7|I Jo 1:7⟧ ⟦1 John 2:9|2:9⟧, ⟦1 John 2:10|10⟧; υἱοὶ (τέκνα) τοῦ φ., ⟦Luke 16:8|Lk 16:8⟧, ⟦John 12:36|Jo 12:36⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:8|Eph 5:8⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:5|I Th 5:5⟧; by meton., of one from whom truth shines forth: ⟦Acts 13:47|Ac 13:47⟧ (LXX), ⟦Romans 2:19|Ro 2:19⟧; esp. of Christ, ⟦Luke 2:32|Lk 2:32⟧, ⟦John 1:7|Jo 1:7⟧, ⟦John 1:8|8⟧ ⟦John 12:35|12:35⟧, ⟦John 12:36|36⟧, ⟦John 12:46|46⟧; τ. φ. τ. κόσμου, ⟦John 8:12|Jo 8:12⟧ ⟦John 9:5|9:5⟧;τ. φ. τ. ἀληθινόν, ⟦John 1:9|Jo 1:9⟧; of Christians, ⟦Matthew 5:14|Mt 5:14⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:8|Eph 5:8⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of the spiritual under­standing: τ. φ. τὸ ἐν σοί, ⟦Matthew 6:23|Mt 6:23⟧, ⟦Luke 11:35|Lk 11:35⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ adverbially, of that which is open to view (opp. to ἐν τ. σκοτίᾳ): ἐν τ. φ., ⟦Matthew 10:27|Mt 10:27⟧, ⟦Luke 12:3|Lk 12:3⟧.†
SYN.: v.s. φέγγος

G5465.b:
⟪χαλάω⟫, -ῶ
[in LXX: (⟦Jeremiah 38:6|Je 45 (38):6⟧) (⁨שׁלח⁩ pi.), etc. ;]
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to slacken, loosen⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to let loose, let go⟫;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to lower, let down⟫: c. acc. rei, ⟦Mark 2:4|Mk 2:4⟧, ⟦Luke 5:4|Lk 5:4, 5⟧, ⟦Acts 9:25|Ac 9:25⟧ ⟦Acts 27:17|27:17⟧, ⟦Acts 27:30|30⟧; c. acc. pers. (cf. ⟦Jeremiah 38:6|Je, l.c.⟧), pass., ⟦2 Corinthians 11:33|II Co 11:33⟧.†

G5467.b:
⟪χαλεπός⟫, -ή, -όν
[in LXX: ⟦Isaiah 18:2|Is 18:2⟧ (⁨נוֺרָא⁩), Wi 3:19, Si 3:21, al. ;] ⟪hard⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪hard to do⟫ or ⟪deal with, difficult⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪hard to bear, painful, grievous⟫: καιροί, ⟦2 Timothy 3:1|II Ti 3:1⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ of persons, ⟪hard to deal with, harsh, fierce, savage⟫: ⟦Matthew 8:28|Mt 8:28⟧.†
